---
title: "How this site composes itself"
date: "2026-10-15"
summary: "Guillotine cuts, weights and a colour cap: the rules behind every section."
tone: "blue"
draft: false
---

Every section is a list of items. The composer splits the space where their weights balance, cuts across the longer side, interleaves small accent fields, and keeps colour under 37.5% of the area.

The cuts are remembered in order, so each composition can assemble on screen the way it was made: heavy lines first, then lighter ones, then the fields.
